i would like to give  ron the opportunity to say a few words  about  why he and his business partner started  the scholarship fund  and allow us all to hear his wisdom  thank you tom i am fully vaccinated and  had coveted in july so i'm going to take  the mask off for a few seconds  it's really an honor to be able to speak  to you here today and to commend  the recipients of this scholarship  award my business partner don and i  used to own a business in town called  planet hyundai  and after the tragic assassination  of officers beck and soldo don and i  met to discuss doing something to show  the department  what the job they do every day means to  us as local business owners  i've been in the tavern business for  over 30 years  so anybody in the las vegas tavern  business knows cops  because they're always stopping by  checking on your staff 24  7. but in the car business don and i  were very lucky to be fortunate with  that investment  and to do well enough that after that  tragic day  i suggested to don that we start a  scholarship fund  in the memory of officers beck and soldo  and that was seven years ago it's hard  to believe  we did a 50 000 offer  um as a result of that i joined the  foundation board  to help decide who would receive the 5  000  scholarships 10 of which this year  there's 12.  and it was one of my happier days of all  the boards i've served on  and businesses i've owned to serve with  the group  such as the las vegas metropolitan  police department foundation board  members  and the work we do to show the officers  of the department  how much we appreciate what they do so  picture us one day thinking what can we  do for cops  cops are used to taking care of  themselves and everyone else  and we came up with the idea to do a  scholarship for their kids  and let them know through gifts to their  children  starting college how much the jobs they  do  mean to us and as i said that was seven  years ago we did fifty thousand dollars  at an  as an initial contribution and as long  as we stayed in the car business we did  that  for six consecutive years awarding a  total of three hundred thousand dollars  and now this year the foundation which  has grown when i joined it  chris and tom we had about a hundred  thousand dollars in the bank  and uh three board members with mike  mcclary  and tom and it's grown significantly  since then to a multi-million dollar  foundation  that this year is funding the twelve  scholarships  as a foundation i'm honored and proud to  be able to say we started it  and and hopefully can continue it  through the  generosity of the community towards the  foundation  so congratulations to the 12 recipients  who i look forward to meeting  individually as we make the awards  and commend you for reaching this height  of  performance that's being rewarded and  maybe  the first financial reward you got for  doing a good job  and as you begin your life in adulthood  you will see many rewards to come for  doing the best job  possible as you did against over 60  competitors for these scholarships so i  commend you  and thank you for making this possible  for me to do  thank you tom  thank you ron we're also honored  today to have the undersheriff with us  the foundation is an independent entity  but works very closely  with the sheriff and then the sheriff to  determine  what are the priorities of funding needs  for the police department  and the community safety initiatives  that the department organizes each and  every year  so it's an honor to have you here under  sheriff and i'll turn the podium over to  you  i just want to make a couple of comments  um you know we talk about the foundation  and you've heard of it obviously and all  that but i think a lot of people don't  realize that it's the people that count  right and it's a it's somebody like ron  corey or don  that started this and it's grown into  the future and what you're seeing behind  me  is the future right you hear on the news  about all the talk about police reform  and how we can do better as we move  forward into the future  it's projects like this that the  foundation undertakes educating our kids  the most important thing we can do is  develop them to be better leaders  and to to help run a business like this  that's going up behind me as we move  forward to be the  leader in america and probably the world  and how we train police officers from  around the country so  while you're here today in this tent on  a nice beautiful sunny day  look back beyond this and realize that  this foundation  supports that type of thing and that  this person where'd he go there he is  this person here really supports the  opportunity for your children to become  leaders  and i hope that they decide to come back  and join our department because we need  them  so thank you for being here  congratulations to all the students  and best of luck in your endeavors in  your college career  and thanks to ron and to don and to tom  and the foundation so  everybody enjoy the day thank you very  much  so as ron pointed out the foundation has  come  quite a long ways in the last five or  six years  raising 100 000 a year was pretty much  what the foundation did for  many years the foundation uh turned 20  years old last year  so that was probably the most that had  been raised in any one year  the last two years we've raised nearly 8  million dollars in each of those years  and that's because of the generosity of  so many community members and  local businesses supporting us and the  only reason they're supporting  us is because each of you who are on the  force  working for the department and working  for the safety of all of us  much of the money that's been raised  over the  last two years is to support the  training facility that  is going up behind us we are in the  first phase of that training project  our goal for the first phase is 25  million and we have fortunately  have received over 18 million in  commitments for that project  and so because of that funding this  project is on track  to be on time and the first building  delivered by the end of the year  and we look forward to celebrating that  on october 1st  later this year because the response  that's required to incidents like what  happened  at the country music festival is exactly  one of the primary reasons for this  training facility  that will not only be used by metro but  other first responder agencies  here in southern nevada and ultimately  throughout the state  so we felt it was only fitting this year  to  allow all of you to have sort of a first  glimpse at what is being done here  and have the opportunity to receive your  scholarships in such an amazing place  in front of a remarkable facility that  is being built  we had this year 60 applicants for this  scholarship  and which is i'm really an incredible  statistic each and every year that  about 60 young people apply for this  and as ron said he uh sits on the  selection committee as i do  and there's probably not a more  challenging task that we face each year  in figuring out of the 60 who should be  the 10 or 12 that we're offering  scholarships to  each year because everyone who applies  is a remarkable young man or woman  who has demonstrated in the essay that  they've submitted  why it has been a rewarding  and meaningful experience to grow up in  a law enforcement household  and part of this effort is to recognize  and  honor your parents who have served  and continue to serve so honorably for  our community  so it is our pleasure to  present each of you with a certificate  today  recognizing your accomplishment as a  2021  alan beck and new dorsaldo memorial  scholarship winner  so congratulations to each and every one  of you  i'm gonna ask ron and the undersheriff  to come up  so that they can congratulate you  and you'll get your photo taken with  them  our first recipient bevalequa  iii congratulations  our next recipient viviana 